---
import Docs from "../../layouts/Docs.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../../components/CodeBlock.astro";
---

<Docs title="Functions" description="Defining functions with parameters, return types and recursion in RUDRA." slug="functions">
  <p class="lead">Functions are declared with <code>fn</code>. Parameters are typed, and a return type is written after an arrow.</p>

  <h2>Parameters and return types</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={`fn add(a: int, b: int) -> int {
    return a + b;
}
fn main() {
    print(add(2, 3));
}`} />

  <h2>Returning early</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={`fn classify(n: int) -> str {
    if n > 0 {
        return "positive";
    } else if n < 0 {
        return "negative";
    } else {
        return "zero";
    }
}
fn main() {
    print(classify(-4));
}`} />

  <h2>Recursion</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={`fn factorial(n: int) -> int {
    if n <= 1 {
        return 1;
    }
    return n * factorial(n - 1);
}
fn main() {
    print(factorial(5));
}`} />
  <p>This program prints <code>120</code>.</p>

  <h2>Procedures</h2>
  <p>A function without a return type performs work without producing a value.</p>
  <CodeBlock code={`fn greet(name: str) {
    print("Hello, " + name);
}
fn main() {
    greet("RUDRA");
}`} />
</Docs>
